WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.540
the three boys put on their wellies

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.620
they ran down the field

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.540
they swam on the swing

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.160
they rolled down the corn cyrcle

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.900
they came to the river

00:00:32.347 --> 00:00:34.127
they sat on the edge

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.660
dangling their feet over the stream

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.440
Look! - said Rupe

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.700
the sandy beach

00:00:42.582 --> 00:00:44.422
sure enough, they saw there

00:00:44.422 --> 00:00:46.382
was little tiny beach of sand

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.560
Terence said

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.040
the land reaches down into the water

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.500
and Rupert said

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.680
no, the water reaches up into the land

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.160
Ralph said - it's both

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.580
water and sand

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.920
it's the sandy beach

00:01:07.569 --> 00:01:09.749
it's a fractal object

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.580
they stood then, they walked in the stream

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.240
Look! - said Terence

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.540
it circles to the left

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.380
No - said Rupert

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.380
it circles to the right

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.420
it"s turbulent flow

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.980
said Ralph - it's a mathematical object

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.360
it's chaos

00:01:32.894 --> 00:01:34.254
on the other side

00:01:35.477 --> 00:01:37.637
of the stream, there was no beach

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.480
there was a concrete wall

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.960
it was not a fractal object

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.500
Rupert said

00:01:47.532 --> 00:01:49.432
it's a straight line

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:51.880
Terence said

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:57.560
it's a Bauhaus excrescent of post-linguistic humanoids

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.360
thinking of peanut-butter sandwiches then, they walked back up the slope

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.380
Rupert said

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.940
nature has given us a lesson

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.320
nature is our teacher

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.570
we have learned about the sandy beach

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.740
the sun had set

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.880
Ralph pointed to the sky

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.400
Look! - he said. They looked and saw

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.980
there was a silver stripe in the sky shining there

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.040
they hadn't noticed it before

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.040
it girduld the entire celestial bolt

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.300
it sprang from two legs

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.440
to the south that way, they saw that

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.980
it's two legs appeared in the zodiacal belt

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:59.440
it sprang across the mid-heaven, going somewhere near the polar constellations

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:02.560
Rupert said

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.340
I think those constellations over there, those are all watery

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.820
there's Pisces, there's fish

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.520
it's biology projected on the sky

00:03:12.844 --> 00:03:17.944
Terence said - the Calvea astrologers called that the celestial sea

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.920
and Ralph said

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.460
it's a sandy beach in the sky

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.520
and Rupe said

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.680
Father Sky is our teacher too

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.200
Ralph said - Well, there's

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.920
a sphere above the sky

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.860
with the sandy beach in it

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.640
and a kind of astral projection

00:03:44.443 --> 00:03:47.403
imprints its shadow on the celestial sphere

00:03:47.403 --> 00:03:50.683
and on the terrestrial disc as well

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.800
they went back to the kitchen and tugged off their wellies

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.460
and looked for peanut-butter in the fridge

